+# Rekor Restore Drill — Detailed Runbook
+
+Objective:
+- Validate backup restore, measure RTO, check integrity, rotate TLS certs, and test client verification post-restore.
+
+Pre-reqs:
+- Backup bucket access (S3/GCS) with retention & latest backup id.
+- Staging RDS instance (db user + pw).
+- cert-manager installed for TLS rotation (or CA access).
+
+Steps:
+1) Announce drill and snapshot current state (timestamp).
+2) Download latest backup: aws s3 cp s3://aegis-rekor-backups/<file> /tmp/rekor.dump
+3) Restore: PGPASSWORD=${STAGING_PG_PASSWORD} pg_restore -h ${STAGING_PG_HOST} -U ${STAGING_PG_USER} -d rekor --clean /tmp/rekor.dump
+4) Rotate TLS cert using cert-manager: apply Certificate CR, wait for secret, restart, validate endpoint.
+5) Restart Rekor deployment and validate /api/v1/log/log_info and sample entry reads.
+6) Measure RTO (end-to-end), check data integrity for sample entries and verify Rekor proofs for known signatures.
+7) Document RTO, any discrepancies, and remediation items in DR binder.
